1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,400
Find the cheapest route that respects resource limits
and never repeats a customer.

2
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:10,200
Time limit: 8. Payload limit: 2. The cost-3 route takes
12 time units: infeasible.

3
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:15,867
The best feasible path is S–B–D–T: cost six, time six,
payload two. Verified by the solver and exhaustive
enumeration.

4
00:00:15,867 --> 00:00:23,833
Bidirectional labeling grows paths from the start and
from the destination, then joins compatible partial
paths.

5
00:00:23,833 --> 00:00:31,200
At the same node, with the same visited set, a label
with no higher cost or resource use can dominate
another.

6
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:38,467
Adaptive buckets group labels by resource use.
Conservative summaries skip impossible comparisons;
surviving labels still receive exact checks.

7
00:00:38,467 --> 00:00:44,067
ESPPRC extends cspy with bucket screening, faster
joins, SRI-aware costs and optional parallel
preparation. Serial remains the default.

8
00:00:44,067 --> 00:00:52,067
Built on cspy by David Torres Sanchez. Subset-row
inequalities: Jepsen, Petersen, Spoorendonk and
Pisinger, 2008. Animation created with 3Blue1Brown’s
ManimGL.
